  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "A high-fat meal makes no clinically significant difference, and it is over 99% bound to plasma protein. Metabolism is split about equally between CYP3A and glucuronidation.",
    "substance": "Formulated as a hydrochloride salt; the active moiety has a molecular weight of 510.6.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA in one 0.75 mg tablet strength, supplied as bottles of 30 tablets.",
    "safety": "Boxed warning for embryo-fetal toxicity; contraindicated in pregnancy and in hypersensitivity to the drug. Peripheral edema and anemia are the most common adverse reactions.",
    "indication": "Reducing proteinuria in adults with primary IgA nephropathy at risk of rapid disease progression.",
    "mechanism": "Blocks the endothelin type A receptor with more than 1800-fold selectivity over the type B receptor."
  },
  "tell": "An endothelin type A receptor antagonist with over 1800-fold selectivity; its boxed warning covers embryo-fetal toxicity.",
